## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical DNS troubleshooting skills, anycast path reasoning, and ability to design a reproducible diagnostic plan with concrete commands.

## Key Concepts

- DNS resolution and TTL behavior
- Anycast routing and cache effects
- Health checks and traffic steering
- Reproducibility and data collection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: parse a dns trace to extract served A record
function extractRegion(traceLines) {
  const line = traceLines.find(l => l.includes('A')) || traceLines[0];
  const match = line.match(/([0-9]{1,3}\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}/);
  return match ? match[0] : null;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate a rollback plan if regional DNS changes cause regression?
- Which metrics signal a successful stabilization?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical diagnostic reasoning for common cross-region latency issues, focusing on DNS routing, TLS termination, and edge pathing rather than code changes.

## Key Concepts

- DNS routing and TTL effects
- TLS handshake timing across regions
- Edge NAT/firewall behavior and LB logs
- Basic network measurement tools (dig, curl, mtr, openssl)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: measure DNS and HTTP timings in Node.js
const https = require('https');
const start = Date.now();
https.get('https://api.example.com/ping', res => {
  res.resume();
  res.on('end', () => console.log('elapsed', Date.now() - start));
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- What are trade-offs between low vs high DNS TTL in this setup, and how would you monitor them?
- How would you validate TLS termination consistency across regions without changing apps?

